<p>If you have been wondering how to make money on Skillshare, the short answer is: you teach short video classes, paying members watch them, and Skillshare sends you a slice of a monthly royalty pool based on those watch minutes. There are no individual sales and no price to set. That makes Skillshare simpler than a marketplace like Udemy, but it also means your income rises and falls with something you cannot fully control: how much of everyone's viewing time lands on your classes.</p>
<p>Below is how Skillshare teacher pay works as of 2026, the new eligibility rules that cut off many small teachers, what earnings look like in practice, the Skillshare affiliate program, and how it stacks up against Udemy. (If you searched for "Shareskill," you are in the right place, as it is a common misspelling.)</p>

