  <li><strong>From the update effective July 16:</strong> you need either <strong>400+ minutes</strong> watched by active members in the month plus at least one new quality class published in the previous 18 months, or <strong>650+ minutes</strong> if you have not published in the last 18 months. The 50-follower minimum still applies.</li>
</ul>
<div class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Watch out:</strong> These thresholds mean a brand-new teacher with one class will usually earn nothing at first. Plan on publishing several classes and actively building followers before you expect a payout. Skillshare has changed teacher pay several times, so check its help center for the latest rules before you invest weeks of work.</div>

<h3 id="referral-bonus">Teacher referral bonus</h3>
<p>Every class comes with a teacher referral link. Skillshare's teacher blog has described paying a <strong>$10 bonus</strong>, added to your next payment, when someone you refer signs up for a membership and makes their first payment. It is not a lot per signup, but if you already have an audience on Instagram, YouTube or TikTok, referrals add up and bring watch minutes to your classes at the same time.</p>

<h2 id="how-much">How much money can you make on Skillshare?</h2>
<p>This is the question everyone asks, and the honest answer is "it varies widely." Skillshare does not publish teacher earnings averages, and per-minute value changes each month. What we can say with confidence:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Most teachers earn little.</strong> A single class with a few hundred monthly minutes may not even clear the payout threshold.</li>
  <li><strong>Catalogs win.</strong> Teachers who publish many classes in one niche, especially creative topics like illustration, Procreate, photography, design and video editing, collect the most minutes.</li>
  <li><strong>Payouts have trended down for many teachers.</strong> Teachers have publicly reported lower earnings after past pay changes, so do not build a budget around last year's numbers.</li>
</ul>
