<h2 id="more-minutes">How to get more watch minutes</h2>
<p>Because every dollar you earn on Skillshare traces back to minutes watched, the whole game is getting members to start your classes and finish them. A few habits make a real difference:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Hook in the first 30 seconds.</strong> Show the finished project or result right away, then explain what students will make. Long personal intros cause drop-off.</li>
  <li><strong>Keep lessons short.</strong> Several short lessons feel easier to keep watching than one long one, and they make it simple for members to pick up where they left off.</li>
  <li><strong>Make the project fun and achievable.</strong> A satisfying project encourages students to finish the class, post their work and follow you for the next one.</li>
  <li><strong>Link your classes together.</strong> Mention your other classes at the end of each one so a member who enjoyed one has an obvious next step.</li>
  <li><strong>Engage in discussions.</strong> Replying to questions and giving project feedback builds the follower count you need for payouts and keeps students coming back.</li>
  <li><strong>Refresh older classes.</strong> Update thumbnails and titles on classes that get views but low completion, and re-record lessons that have aged badly.</li>
</ul>
<p>None of this requires expensive gear. It requires treating each class like a small product, studying what your own analytics say about where viewers stop, and fixing those spots.</p>

